      "side": 1,
      "message": "This isn\u0027t correct for advanced cases like the system partition. For the system partition, you\u0027re passing the SYSTEM/ subdirectory, but build_image should really run on the \"root\" files with the \"system\" files as a subdirectory of the root.\n\nI think it\u0027s complicated and errorprone to try and rebuild the partitions in a different module type. I liked the previous architecture of having the filesystem module output both a hermetic and non-hermetic image, could we keep that? We just need to do the build_image command in a separate RuleBuilder from the staging directory so that both build_image commands can reuse the same staging directory.",
      "revId": "2b7c4b466c94d2b8307d86aefdb906e6ef4d0000",
